          "code": "OUTPUT_FORMAT",
          "id": "1768570787503",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768570787504_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Model Data:\n{{$context.$nodes.DATA_ASSESSEMENT.$output}}\n\nShow Title as \"Available attributes with sufficient data density are matched to the model requirements. Additional models may become available as the data gets enriched\".\n\nDisplay a list of available models in a tabular layout.\n\nEach row represents one Model.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nStep 1: Define Fields\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n1) Model\n   - Value: name of the model derived from the data assessment output.\n   - This field must uniquely identify the model per row.\n   - Show Model name in full form E.g Next Best Offer Instead of NBO\n\n2) Data availability\n   - Value format:\n     \"<PASSED>/<TOTAL> attributes with <THRESHOLD> availability\"\n   - PASSED = number of attributes that meet the minimum density.\n   - TOTAL = total number of required attributes for that model.\n   - THRESHOLD = the minimum density threshold mentioned in the data assessment output (do NOT hard code).\n3) Status \nIf <PASSED> = <TOTAL>\n→ Display a Green circle with the text “Ready”\n\nOtherwise\n→ Display a Red circle with the text “Not Ready”\n--------------------------------------------------\nStep 2: Action\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nFor each row generate an action exactly as below.\nThe action must be attached to the row and must NOT be rendered as a column or text.\n\nora.Invoke(\"CreateModel\", {\n  \"action\": \"CreateModel\",\n  \"model\": \"<Model>\",\n  \"label\": \"Create <Model>\"\n})\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOutput Rules\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- Overall title should be \"Available attributes with sufficient data density are matched to the model requirements. Additional models may become available as the data gets enriched\".\n- Do NOT make up model data.\n- If there is no data in Model Data, display an empty list.\n- Output strictly as a structured list dataset.\n- Do NOT output JSON manually.\n- Do NOT stringify or embed actions inside fields.\n- Do NOT mention widget names or component types.\n- Do NOT include explanations or extra text."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "Input\n\nModel Data:\n{{ $context.$nodes.DATA_ASSESSEMENT.$output.result }}\n\nDisplay Rules\n\nShow a short title indicating models that are ready for quick wins based on data availability.\n\nDisplay the results in a clean tabular layout.\n\nEach row represents one model extracted from the Data Assessment output.\n\nStep 1: Define Fields\n\nFor each model, display the following columns:\n\n1) Model\n\nValue: Model name from the Data Assessment result.\n\n2) Data Availability\n\nFormat:\n\"<PASSED>/<TOTAL> attributes with <THRESHOLD> availability\"\n\nWhere:\n\nPASSED = number of attributes meeting minimum density\n\nTOTAL = total required attributes\n\nTHRESHOLD = minimum density threshold\n\nDo not hardcode any values. Always extract from input.\n\nStep 2: Action\n\nFor each row, generate exactly one action:\n\nora.Invoke(\"CreateModel\", {\n  \"action\": \"CreateModel\",\n  \"model\": \"<Model>\"\n})\n\n\nReplace <Model> dynamically with the model name.\n\nOutput Rules\n\nDo NOT hardcode model names, thresholds, or counts.\n\nDo NOT return JSON as the final output.\n\nDo NOT add explanations or commentary.\n\nOutput only the final formatted text/table.\n\nAssume UI will render the table and the action buttons.\n\nIf you want, share a sample DATA_ASSESSEMENT output JSON, and I will generate the final working output so you can test it in Fusion.\n\nFusion app section here is the output and {\n\"assessmentLevel\": \"Algorithm\",\n\"minReqDensity\": 50,\n\"summary\": [\n{\n\"model\": \"NBO\",\n\"totalMandatory\": 5,\n\"sufficient\": 3,\n\"availability\": \"3/5 attributes with >=50% availability\",\n\"verdict\": \"NOT READY\"\n}\n]\n}\nwant to dispaly as table format .. how i can disply as a table format .. tel me the instructions \n\nHere is the exact instruction you must give Fusion so that the output renders as a table in the Agent UI.\n\nFusion’s renderer creates tables automatically when you output a simple Markdown table — nothing else will work reliably.\n\n✅ Use this instruction inside your Output Formatter\n\nCopy–paste this into the Output Format prompt:\n\nINSTRUCTION TO RENDER TABLE FROM DATA ASSESSMENT OUTPUT\n\nYou are formatting the Data Assessment result into a clean table.\n\nUse the following structure:",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
